{"t": 3098.886, "n": 393, "ev": "result", "ok": true, "text": "The preview didn't complete, so I can't confirm the gate result, and I'm stopping here. The disk holding `/tmp/claude-1000` has 0 MB free. The restarted `tempergraph self-check` exited with code 120 and no output. Even `git status` now fails with a disk-full error, so I can't confirm the tree state either.\n\nI haven't deleted anything to make room. Freeing space on that volume is your call. Setting `CLAUDE_CODE_TMPDIR` to a directory on another volume would also work. The full pytest run took about 19 minutes last time, and its output and temp folders may be what filled the disk.\n\n**What I changed**\n- **Cause of the earlier failure:** the three failing tests never isolated `HOME`, so on a host with a cached claude sign-in they saw `interactive_login`. This task doesn't touch `schedule/`. I reproduced one failure first (`assert (0 == 2)`).\n- **Test-only fix:** I made the same `HOME` isolation `test_schedule_credentials.py` already uses in the three test files. They are `tests/test_schedule_fire.py`, `tests/test_schedule_export.py` and `tests/test_schedule_tick.py`.\n  - These files are named by no plan row. The report lists them as a deviation.\n  - `-n 0` runs of the three files passed, and `ruff check src tests` was clean.\n- **Not checked at the base:** I didn't run the three tests at the base commit, so \"failed before this task\" is my reading of the code path, not an observation.\n- **Rule files:** I opened `task-notes.rule.md` and `plan.rule.md` with the read tool this session.\n- **Plan and report:** every plan row is marked and the status is `completed`. I rewrote `plugins/tempergraph/docs/tasks/i21b.report.md` to describe this.\n\n**Not verified**\n- I haven't seen a full `python -m pytest` pass. The three fixed tests pass alone, but the full suite and the other preview commands have not run to a result.\n- The live P-CC-13 test needs `TEMPERGRAPH_LIVE=1` and a signed-in `claude`. It has not run.\n\nOnce space is freed, `tempergraph self-check 8b97713c554e0423fcd3d856d5191049` needs to run once more on the unchanged tree. The first thing to check is `git status`, because the disk-full error may have cut off a write.\n\nARTIFACT code_report: plugins/tempergraph/docs/tasks/i21b.report.md\nARTIFACT tests_passed: no\nBLOCKED: the disk holding /tmp/claude-1000 is full (0 MB free). A person must free space or set CLAUDE_CODE_TMPDIR to another volume. Then the preview needs one run on the unchanged tree, and `git status` needs a check first.", "subtype": "success", "is_error": false, "session_id": "6beec69a-19bc-4afb-8e7a-9c93f924f3e8"}
